  "notes": [
    "The campaign brief quotes r_c = R(1-tau_y/tau_w); the plug relation is r_c = R*tau_y/tau_w and R(1-tau_y/tau_w) is the yielded-annulus thickness. Both are reported.",
    "A regularised yield-stress model has no perfectly rigid plug: the core creeps at sigma/nu_plug, which is why the plug probe is compared both to the ideal H-B profile and to the exact 1-D solution of the regularised model.",
    "Pure plane Couette has a uniform stress, hence no interior yield surface; that degeneracy is the N2 negative control rather than a missing capability."
  ],
